WEBVTT

00:08.690 --> 00:16.160
aozameta machinami yureru boku no kage

00:08.690 --> 00:16.160
The pale street, my swaying shadow,

00:16.160 --> 00:24.440
nibui ashidori wa yuku saki wo shirazu

00:16.160 --> 00:24.440
I walk slowly, not knowing my destination.

00:24.440 --> 00:30.480
kawasenu omoi

00:24.440 --> 00:30.480
My feelings can't reach yours.

00:31.240 --> 00:38.620
kimi no hitomi no naka utsushidasu mono wo

00:31.240 --> 00:38.620
The things reflected in the depths of your eyes,

00:38.620 --> 00:46.860
uketomeru tame ni hashiridashiteita

00:38.620 --> 00:46.860
I started running in order to catch up to them.

00:46.860 --> 01:00.640
sashidasu sono te wo hodokerai youni nigirikaesu

00:46.860 --> 01:00.640
I grip your outstretched hand without letting go.

01:01.170 --> 01:08.680
hanbun no tsuki no yoru wa bokura wo terashite

01:01.170 --> 01:08.680
On this night, the half moon shines upon us.

01:08.680 --> 01:15.990
oikaketekita jikan wo boku wa furikitte

01:08.680 --> 01:15.990
I shake off the flow of time chasing after us.

01:16.220 --> 01:27.430
hanbun zutsu no bokura wa egaku saki made mo mieru

01:16.220 --> 01:27.430
We're half of ourselves, but we can draw the future.

02:08.610 --> 02:12.380
Ezaki Collection's Demise... And...

02:19.820 --> 02:21.720
Ah, it's you.

02:21.720 --> 02:23.720
You should lock your window.

02:24.320 --> 02:25.220
It's dangerous like this.

02:25.220 --> 02:26.790
That may be true...

02:26.790 --> 02:29.390
But I didn't know when you'd show up, so...

02:32.430 --> 02:33.030
Come on!

02:34.830 --> 02:35.530
What?

02:35.530 --> 02:36.630
Damn it!

02:36.630 --> 02:37.800
Alright!

02:39.640 --> 02:40.840
Yuuichi...

02:40.840 --> 02:42.170
Did something happen?

02:42.870 --> 02:44.080
What do you mean?

02:44.510 --> 02:46.680
I don't know, that's why I asked you.

02:47.280 --> 02:48.710
Nothing happened.

02:49.510 --> 02:51.020
Then it's okay...

02:53.120 --> 02:55.950
Idiot, you don't have to be so serious.

02:58.590 --> 03:01.360
Really, nothing happened at all.

03:06.160 --> 03:07.230
Tsukasa?

03:07.230 --> 03:08.030
What is it?

03:08.330 --> 03:10.800
That time when we became friends...

03:11.940 --> 03:12.970
Do you still remember it?

03:14.810 --> 03:17.840
Weren't we good friends the moment we saw each other?

03:18.440 --> 03:20.510
You sure are a good guy.

03:26.950 --> 03:29.520
Lightning in this season?

03:30.190 --> 03:32.890
It is supposed to rain tonight.

03:42.070 --> 03:43.970
Where are you going, Yuuichi?

03:47.410 --> 03:49.140
Storage room

03:52.510 --> 03:54.150
Is there anything like a rope here?

04:01.420 --> 04:02.690
Hey, Tsukasa.

04:02.690 --> 04:04.020
Take one end of the rope.

04:05.090 --> 04:07.130
What's with that mask?

04:07.130 --> 04:08.260
No...

04:08.260 --> 04:12.160
I'm afraid people will see me coming into a hospital without permission...

04:13.530 --> 04:14.670
I'm going down.

04:22.510 --> 04:24.380
Tsukasa, hold onto this end of the rope.

04:24.380 --> 04:25.780
Don't do it...

04:25.780 --> 04:27.280
It's dangerous.

04:27.280 --> 04:30.480
That book, I can't let it get wet.

04:49.870 --> 04:51.470
Are you okay, Yuuichi?

04:51.470 --> 04:52.740
I-I think so.

05:04.980 --> 05:07.320
Demon's Windmill Shield!

05:07.320 --> 05:09.190
Tsukasa, are you okay?

05:09.450 --> 05:10.820
I'm holding on...

05:11.220 --> 05:14.790
Yuuichi, hurry up and climb back.

05:14.790 --> 05:15.830
Y-Yeah!

05:56.100 --> 05:57.700
Sekoguchi!

05:57.700 --> 05:58.870
Ezaki-kun?

06:01.670 --> 06:02.670
Let me help you.

06:03.040 --> 06:04.440
I can't take it back home with me...

06:04.940 --> 06:07.310
But to help you find a home for it, that I can still do.

06:11.520 --> 06:13.580
Why is it like this?

06:13.920 --> 06:15.590
How many degrees is it?

06:15.590 --> 06:16.820
39 degrees.

06:18.760 --> 06:19.990
Let's measure it one more time.

06:30.470 --> 06:32.970
Go! Yuuichi!

06:33.370 --> 06:36.170
Like that! It's close! Hurry!

06:41.680 --> 06:44.080
Alright! Number one!

06:44.080 --> 06:46.380
Congratulations, Yuuichi!

06:46.380 --> 06:49.090
Good job, kid.

06:49.520 --> 06:50.820
Tsukasa!

06:50.820 --> 06:51.690
Tada-san!

06:52.260 --> 06:57.030
Kid, use the same kind of strength and run towards her!

06:57.760 --> 06:58.760
Rika?

06:59.460 --> 07:00.470
Yuuichi.

07:01.670 --> 07:02.800
Rika...

07:03.770 --> 07:05.070
Damn...

07:05.070 --> 07:06.640
That's too cute...

07:07.670 --> 07:08.740
Rika,

07:08.740 --> 07:12.080
some day after the operation when you've recovered,

07:12.080 --> 07:13.680
let's go somewhere far away.

07:14.010 --> 07:14.780
Okay.

07:14.780 --> 07:17.450
Oh right, why don't we take some box lunch to the ocean?

07:17.820 --> 07:19.780
Have you ever been to the ocean before?

07:19.780 --> 07:20.650
I haven't.

07:20.890 --> 07:23.120
Then I'll take you there.

07:23.820 --> 07:25.560
Just like last time when we went to Mt. Houdai.

07:27.430 --> 07:28.860
Hey, Yuuichi...

07:29.390 --> 07:31.460
Why did you help me get that book back?

07:44.180 --> 07:47.450
That book was given to you by your father, right?

07:48.050 --> 07:48.680
Yeah.

07:50.110 --> 07:52.850
You'd be really sad if it got wet, right?

07:54.450 --> 07:55.090
Yeah.

07:57.620 --> 07:58.990
I'm sorry, Rika...

07:59.590 --> 08:00.260
I...

08:00.260 --> 08:01.660
didn't know what I was saying...

08:01.930 --> 08:02.860
No...

08:03.290 --> 08:05.160
I lied as well.

08:06.130 --> 08:08.230
Even if Natsume-sensei didn't tell me to...

08:08.730 --> 08:11.670
I still would've wanted to make up with you.

08:19.140 --> 08:20.440
What a relief...

08:20.810 --> 08:22.080
This feels like a dream.

08:23.950 --> 08:26.920
I see, this is a dream.

08:27.450 --> 08:29.550
Get some rest.

08:37.060 --> 08:39.060
Thank you, Yuuichi.

08:45.300 --> 08:47.810
Note: Akiba Rika

08:54.480 --> 08:55.810
What are you doing?

09:00.020 --> 09:01.090
U-Uh...

09:01.090 --> 09:02.020
Rika!

09:02.020 --> 09:03.120
How strange.

09:03.520 --> 09:05.120
Standing in front of my doorway...

09:05.120 --> 09:06.420
What were you planning to do?

09:06.420 --> 09:07.860
S-Sorry...

09:07.860 --> 09:09.230
Hey, come on in.

09:14.630 --> 09:15.770
What is this?

09:15.770 --> 09:17.440
That one is really tasty!

09:17.440 --> 09:18.300
Do you want to try?

09:19.700 --> 09:20.970
Then, throw it to me!

09:24.740 --> 09:26.710
What are you so happy about?

09:26.710 --> 09:28.580
Because I caught it.

09:28.580 --> 09:31.580
Of course you did. The distance is so short.

09:32.120 --> 09:33.950
Hmm, how boring...

09:33.950 --> 09:36.790
Why can't you say "Nice catch" or something...

09:38.690 --> 09:39.720
It's okay.

09:40.490 --> 09:42.030
I understand.

09:43.030 --> 09:53.270
Note: Night on the Galactic Railroad - Miyazawa Kenji

09:43.760 --> 09:47.360
I went to your room and found you sleeping with a fever.

09:47.730 --> 09:50.470
Going out to get the book in the rain...

09:50.800 --> 09:52.840
Seriously, how stupid.

09:53.600 --> 09:54.840
Here, this is for you.

09:56.040 --> 09:57.110
Nice catch!

09:59.540 --> 10:00.910
You're an idiot.

10:00.910 --> 10:02.610
What is it?

10:04.620 --> 10:05.780
So then...

10:05.780 --> 10:07.350
You went to my room before?

10:07.620 --> 10:08.190
Huh?

10:09.250 --> 10:10.120
Ah...

10:10.120 --> 10:11.090
It's nothing...

10:11.760 --> 10:12.790
Was that...

10:12.790 --> 10:14.230
not a dream?

10:17.330 --> 10:19.660
Good bye, young cuties...

10:19.660 --> 10:21.400
Super cute...

10:21.930 --> 10:24.600
Good bye, big-breasted girls...

10:24.600 --> 10:26.640
Super sexy...

10:27.840 --> 10:30.210
Good bye, glassed-girl fever...

10:32.840 --> 10:35.150
Sorry, Tada-san.

10:35.810 --> 10:37.220
What are you doing?

10:37.680 --> 10:39.050
Natsume-sensei?

10:39.050 --> 10:40.420
Oh! What's this?

10:40.420 --> 10:41.720
These are all adult books?

10:42.050 --> 10:43.860
Someone else gave them to me.

10:44.090 --> 10:45.590
Incredible!

10:45.890 --> 10:47.960
So this is Ezaki's legendary collection.

10:47.960 --> 10:49.790
It's Tada's collection.

10:50.260 --> 10:52.330
Rika told me to burn them.

10:53.330 --> 10:56.400
If I burn all of them, she'll forgive me.

10:58.400 --> 10:59.670
Eh?

11:00.200 --> 11:04.340
That dumping-a-meal-on-someone-incident Rika forgave you that easily?

11:04.340 --> 11:06.480
"Dumping a meal on someone incident"?

11:06.480 --> 11:07.810
In my old hospital...

11:08.380 --> 11:11.580
One of my co-workers got Rika annoyed.

11:12.580 --> 11:15.290
Guess what Rika did to my co-worker.

11:15.650 --> 11:16.650
I wouldn't know...

11:17.520 --> 11:19.790
She threw a pen on the floor,

11:19.790 --> 11:22.530
and when my co-worker went to pick it up,

11:22.530 --> 11:25.260
a big bowl was dropped on my co-worker's head.

11:25.860 --> 11:29.200
After that, miso soup came raining down.

11:29.200 --> 11:33.070
All the other dishes were thrown one by one too.

11:33.600 --> 11:36.010
Ah, but the pudding was somehow saved.

11:36.010 --> 11:37.240
Can you believe that?

11:37.240 --> 11:39.740
If it's Rika, it's not unbelievable...

11:39.740 --> 11:42.080
My co-worker didn't know what to do at the time...

11:42.510 --> 11:45.750
So, as Rika's chief physician, I got complained to.

11:46.480 --> 11:48.790
For Rika to actually forgive you...

11:50.360 --> 11:52.760
What did you do?

11:58.600 --> 11:59.460
What is it?

12:00.530 --> 12:02.170
No, it's nothing...

12:02.830 --> 12:04.840
Ezaki Yuuchi

12:05.370 --> 12:09.540
"With his lips puckered in a lonely expression as though he were whistling, Giovanni...

12:09.540 --> 12:13.850
came down the sloping dark cypress-lined street."

12:14.250 --> 12:15.950
Yo, Romeo.

12:16.350 --> 12:18.550
What's with the Romeo?

12:18.550 --> 12:20.350
Rika-chan is calling for you.

12:20.720 --> 12:21.720
For me?

12:21.950 --> 12:23.720
Yup, you.

12:25.220 --> 12:27.060
How troublesome.

12:27.060 --> 12:30.230
Then I'll go tell her, "Yuuichi is busy at the moment."

12:31.230 --> 12:32.860
No, it's okay.

12:32.860 --> 12:33.970
Eh?

12:33.970 --> 12:35.200
It's fine!

12:35.200 --> 12:37.000
You don't have to be so polite.

12:37.240 --> 12:39.300
I don't have anything to do anyway.

12:40.710 --> 12:41.940
So you're going?

12:44.410 --> 12:46.740
Akiko-san, do you know how to whistle?

12:47.410 --> 12:48.610
Whistle?

12:51.120 --> 12:52.880
That's very good.

12:53.250 --> 12:56.420
It acts as signals when I'm on the bike.

12:56.420 --> 12:57.020
Huh?

12:57.020 --> 13:01.190
Like "I'm making a U-turn,"  "Go" or "You're dead."

13:01.190 --> 13:02.930
That's enough...

13:03.460 --> 13:04.260
Yuuichi.

13:05.260 --> 13:06.400
What is it?

13:07.400 --> 13:10.030
Remember to be gentle with Rika-chan.

13:13.340 --> 13:14.470
How do you feel?

13:14.770 --> 13:15.970
I'm fine.

13:16.270 --> 13:17.280
I see.

13:17.280 --> 13:18.010
Have you taken a walk yet?

13:18.410 --> 13:19.540
Today, not yet.

13:20.240 --> 13:23.380
Don't force yourself, just try to walk a bit more each day.

13:23.380 --> 13:25.380
Then, open up.

13:27.250 --> 13:28.150
What is it?

13:28.150 --> 13:30.090
No, it's nothing.

13:35.130 --> 13:39.460
The weather is still a bit cold.
Be careful not to get a cold when you're walking.

13:39.460 --> 13:40.100
Okay.

13:46.170 --> 13:47.640
Yuuichi, are you there?

13:47.640 --> 13:48.970
Ah, yeah.

13:54.150 --> 13:56.050
Acting so suspiciously...

14:02.150 --> 14:03.020
Are you okay?

14:03.020 --> 14:04.660
Do you want to rest for a bit?

14:04.660 --> 14:05.790
I'm fine.

14:05.790 --> 14:06.720
Let's go.

14:06.720 --> 14:08.160
A-Alright.

14:09.160 --> 14:11.330
Don't worry, "Giovanni".

14:13.630 --> 14:15.630
Is that so, "Campanella"?

14:15.630 --> 14:16.570
It is.

14:20.040 --> 14:23.470
"I've really come to the fields of Heaven."

14:23.840 --> 14:26.380
Was that a quotation from
"Night on the Galactic Railroad" too?

14:26.380 --> 14:27.280
That's right.

14:27.510 --> 14:29.780
You sure remember it well.

14:30.150 --> 14:31.980
I read it a lot, that's why.

14:31.980 --> 14:32.680
Look,

14:34.090 --> 14:35.590
"The fields of Heaven!"

14:47.230 --> 14:50.540
Doctor, please don't smoke here.

14:50.540 --> 14:52.240
It's cigarette-shaped chocolate.

14:52.240 --> 14:53.100
Yeah, yeah...

14:53.100 --> 14:54.610
Please don't smoke over here.

14:54.610 --> 14:56.770
I said this is only cigarette-shaped chocolate.

14:56.770 --> 14:58.180
Natsume-sensei?

15:00.410 --> 15:01.650
I've been waiting for you.

15:06.080 --> 15:07.850
It's so warm.

15:07.850 --> 15:10.590
It'll be spring in another one to two months.

15:10.590 --> 15:12.090
Spring?

15:12.090 --> 15:13.730
When the weather gets warmer,

15:13.730 --> 15:15.630
let's sneak out of the hospital,

15:15.630 --> 15:17.600
and go to that river over there.

15:17.600 --> 15:19.360
There's a row of sakura trees over there.

15:19.360 --> 15:21.100
They're really pretty!

15:21.100 --> 15:22.830
Ah! I want to go! I want to go!

15:22.830 --> 15:23.700
Take me there!

15:24.000 --> 15:24.700
Of course.

15:25.770 --> 15:29.440
"I wonder if my mother will forgive me."

15:32.580 --> 15:38.520
"I would do anything to bring about my mother's happiness,

15:38.520 --> 15:42.720
but I just can't figure out what would be best to make her happy."

15:42.720 --> 15:46.260
"At least there's nothing wrong with your mother."

15:46.260 --> 15:49.890
"I don't know, but if everyone does..."

15:49.890 --> 15:53.630
"What is good, they create happiness around them, right?"

15:53.970 --> 15:57.700
"That's why I'm sure my mother will forgive me."

15:57.700 --> 15:59.800
You sure remember it well.

16:02.010 --> 16:07.010
"Campanella looked like he had really made up his mind about something."

16:08.280 --> 16:11.220
"We'll be at Cygnus Station soon!"

16:13.320 --> 16:13.990
"Yeah,

16:13.990 --> 16:16.490
we'll pull in at eleven o'clock on the button."

17:02.470 --> 17:03.400
Yo!

17:03.840 --> 17:05.370
What are you doing?

17:13.650 --> 17:15.810
Sneaking off?

17:15.810 --> 17:18.650
You're way too energetic.

17:18.650 --> 17:20.490
Were you drinking?

17:20.490 --> 17:22.250
Aren't you still working?

17:22.250 --> 17:25.020
I don't get drunk of a little sip.

17:25.720 --> 17:26.420
Come with me for a bit.

17:26.420 --> 17:28.260
Wh-What is it?

17:29.030 --> 17:31.500
I want to get some fresh air. Accompany me.

17:33.260 --> 17:35.430
Ezaki, do you want a sip?

17:35.430 --> 17:36.500
Well...

17:36.500 --> 17:37.300
But...

17:38.300 --> 17:39.700
Right, you're underage.

17:39.700 --> 17:40.740
I have hepatitis.

17:45.010 --> 17:46.340
Hey, you.

17:46.340 --> 17:47.550
You are really happy, eh?

17:47.550 --> 17:48.250
Huh?

17:49.050 --> 17:51.650
It's all over your face, your happiness.

17:52.350 --> 17:54.190
Rika is a beauty.

17:54.190 --> 17:55.290
Yeah...

17:55.890 --> 17:58.920
Seventeen-years old, a blossoming girl.

17:58.920 --> 18:01.860
To be able to live with such a cute girl,

18:01.860 --> 18:03.960
that should be enough to make you happy.

18:04.960 --> 18:07.670
I'm similar, so I understand.

18:09.770 --> 18:12.370
But it's just an illusion.

18:12.370 --> 18:14.770
Things like this will be over before you know it.

18:14.770 --> 18:16.970
As an adult, you're jealous of me?

18:18.640 --> 18:19.880
You...

18:19.880 --> 18:20.980
don't understand.

18:21.250 --> 18:22.710
How do I not understand?

18:22.710 --> 18:24.450
You can't get used to looking at me!

18:25.720 --> 18:28.350
I'm always at Rika's side, so...

18:29.750 --> 18:31.590
What are you doing?

18:31.590 --> 18:32.620
You...

18:33.060 --> 18:34.330
don't understand!

18:34.330 --> 18:36.730
I said I understand!

18:36.730 --> 18:37.700
You...

18:47.940 --> 18:49.570
You brat!

18:49.570 --> 18:51.980
How can you be so optimistic?

18:52.410 --> 18:54.680
How can you laugh so foolishly?!

18:57.220 --> 19:00.390
Do you think everything will go so smoothly?

19:01.620 --> 19:03.660
Will the illness be cured just by crying?

19:03.660 --> 19:05.160
Will it be cured just by laughing?

19:05.760 --> 19:08.430
Hope is like garbage.

19:08.430 --> 19:10.360
And you cling to it with all your might.

19:15.500 --> 19:19.340
You haven't had your specialist license test,

19:19.340 --> 19:20.610
haven't written a paper...

19:20.610 --> 19:23.240
Haven't seen the wrath of the professor.

19:38.790 --> 19:39.990
Damn it.

19:42.890 --> 19:46.730
"Campanella, it's back to just the two of us again."

19:47.370 --> 19:49.600
"Let's go on forever together."

19:50.200 --> 19:52.370
"If I could be like that scorpion,

19:52.370 --> 19:55.210
and do something for everyone's benefit,

19:55.210 --> 19:57.980
I wouldn't care if my body burnt up a hundred times over."

19:58.580 --> 20:00.580
"Yeah, I feel the same way."

20:00.880 --> 20:04.580
"But I wonder what true happiness really is."

20:05.080 --> 20:06.580
"I don't know."

20:09.090 --> 20:11.560
"What are you talking about? Get a hold of yourself."

20:12.160 --> 20:16.860
"Oh, there's the Coal Sack! It's a hole in the sky!"

20:17.360 --> 20:21.070
"Even if I were in the middle of that huge darkness, I wouldn't be afraid."

20:21.570 --> 20:24.400
"I really am going to find out what will make people happy."

20:24.870 --> 20:28.370
"Let's go on together, on and on forever."

20:29.270 --> 20:32.310
Yeah, Rika. Let's go on together.

20:39.720 --> 20:43.390
"A boy fell in the river."

20:44.760 --> 20:48.890
"Giovanni, Campanella went in the river!"

20:51.560 --> 20:57.240
"It's no use, it's been minutes since he went in."

20:58.070 --> 21:00.340
Don't worry, "Giovanni".

21:00.810 --> 21:03.070
How can you be so optimistic?

21:03.540 --> 21:06.240
Do you think everything will go so smoothly?

21:22.190 --> 21:25.460
The heart valve's tissues are becoming very weak...

21:25.460 --> 21:28.730
As you can see, the outline is even fuzzier than before.

21:29.400 --> 21:33.640
I'm afraid that the tissues around the heart are fattening because of it.

21:34.640 --> 21:38.310
The possibility of it improving by itself is none.

21:39.880 --> 21:44.620
There are cases where the patient has lived to 30 without the operation.

21:44.980 --> 21:48.350
But your daughter's defect is deteriorating too fast.

21:48.790 --> 21:49.590
Umm...

21:50.150 --> 21:52.920
Can Rika still be saved?

21:54.530 --> 21:56.330
I'll do everything within my power.

21:56.330 --> 21:58.660
The success rate of the operation?

22:38.240 --> 22:47.710
nee, yubisaki de anata wo kanjite

22:38.240 --> 22:47.710
Hey, I felt you with my fingers.

22:50.320 --> 22:59.860
nee, anata to miteita kono keshiki

22:50.320 --> 22:59.860
Hey, while seeing this view together.

23:03.360 --> 23:13.170
tsutawaru yasashisa ni mi wo yudanete

23:03.360 --> 23:13.170
And then I committed myself to your kindness.

23:13.170 --> 23:24.520
eien nado nai wakatte ita tsumori dayo

23:13.170 --> 23:24.520
I know nothing lasts forever.

23:27.720 --> 23:33.690
namae wo yobu anata no koe wo

23:27.720 --> 23:39.660
I will keep your voice, which calls my name, in the bottom of my heart,

23:33.690 --> 23:39.660
mune no oku ni shimatte oku kara

23:39.660 --> 23:45.770
hirakareta tobira no mukou gawa de

23:39.660 --> 23:45.770
On the other side of the open door,

23:45.770 --> 23:52.980
koborenu youni kienai youni

23:45.770 --> 23:52.980
That it won't overflow, it won't disappear.

24:01.120 --> 24:06.290
Next Episode

24:03.050 --> 24:04.790
Even after realizing the truth,

24:05.290 --> 24:08.390
everything stays as it is.

24:09.090 --> 24:12.030
But reality is too heavy to carry...

24:12.760 --> 24:16.100
And I have no power to change it.

24:17.100 --> 24:18.200
Friends...

24:18.200 --> 24:19.070
School...

24:19.070 --> 24:19.970
Pictures...

24:19.970 --> 24:20.870
Memories...

24:21.410 --> 24:24.580
Enjoying every day to the fullest.

24:25.440 --> 24:26.080
Next time,

24:26.080 --> 24:29.710
Looking up at the Half Moon: School Life for Just One Day.

24:28.010 --> 24:31.150
School Life for Just One Day
